# What `docker build -f apps/api/Dockerfile .` (and `-f apps/worker/Dockerfile .`,
# `-f apps/pilot/Dockerfile .`) may not see. Each Dockerfile copies only its
# own app, the workspace packages it runs and the workspace manifests, so
# everything here is either a secret,
# a build output, another tool's state, or bulk the image has no use for. The
# web app is left out whole but for its manifest, which the frozen-lockfile
# check reads.
.git
.github
.claude
**/node_modules
.env
.env.*
**/.next
**/out
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.DS_Store
docs
e2e
supabase
test-results
playwright-report
.playwright-cli
.playwright-mcp
.superpowers
.windsurf
**/*.md
apps/web/**
!apps/web/package.json
# The DAWA snapshot, reference data for an import that has not been written.
packages/db/reference
# Tests, which run in CI and have no reader in the image.
**/__tests__
**/*.test.ts
# The recipes themselves: BuildKit reads each beside the context, not from it.
apps/api/Dockerfile
apps/worker/Dockerfile
apps/pilot/Dockerfile
.dockerignore
